ytic_function_21857cee_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Suppose $f$ and $g$ are real analytic on an open set $E$. Which function is real analytic on $E$ by the listed closure properties?","options":["$|f-g|$ in every possible case","A function defined only on the endpoints of $E$","A function unrelated to $f$ and $g$","$f+g$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a7cdead60c6ac4798b71855f","time_limit":35,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_real_analytic_function_21857cee_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"A power series centred at $a$ converges to $f$ on $(a-r,a+r)\\subseteq E$. What can be said about convergence on a closed subinterval of $(a-r,a+r)$?","options":["It is uniform convergence","It is always divergent","It is pointwise only and never uniform","It is unrelated to the power series"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1563fd715c39d73b4ee2607b","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_real_analytic_function_21857cee_009","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which statement best captures the difference between real analytic and merely infinitely differentiable?","options":["Infinitely differentiable functions are never continuous.","Real analytic functions need not have any derivatives","The two notions are identical by definition","Analytic functions equal a local power series; smooth ones need not."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1d5acccb1c73caf2b9f265cc","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_real_analytic_function_21857cee_010","difficulty":"c